[2m[2mSession[0m: [1;33mollama_minimax-m2.7_cloud-integration-bug-trial-2[0m[0m
All runs clean — no errors. Here's what was fixed:

**`inventory.py`**: Added `asyncio.Lock()` to `decrement` — prevents TOCTOU race where two coroutines both pass the stock check before either decrements.

**`payments.py`**: Added `_charged_orders` set — makes `charge` idempotent. If an order was already charged (payment retry after failure), subsequent attempts return `True` immediately without double-charging.

**`checkout.py`**: Reversed the order — `decrement` first (atomically reserves stock), then `charge`. If payment fails, `increment` restores the reserved stock. This ensures:
- No inventory goes negative (lock serializes all decrements)
- No ghost charges (no charge unless inventory was successfully decremented first)
- No duplicate charges (idempotent `charge` via order tracking)
